{
  "expand": "renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations",
  "id": "10247",
  "self": "https://simeoncalixte1990.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10247",
  "key": "AIN-18",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "[Gap][Finance] Pin a common financial revision across workbench, pricing, quotes and servicing",
    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Finance completion audit \u2014 2026-11-01. Planning priority P1. Evidence classification: code-reviewed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Observed behavior / current model"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Compute reads CanonicalSubmission.data; quotes freeze saved workbench sections; bindings freeze signing snapshots; commercial entries reference commercial revisions. These histories exist but no common financial dependency manifest was demonstrated."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Required change / expected behavior"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Link approved financial revisions and their source hashes across these existing stores; invalidate dependent calculations on material corrections."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Acceptance criteria"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletList",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A currency/premium correction identifies all stale quotes and computations."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Restore/replay selects the same inputs without rewriting old quotes or posted entries."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Verification and boundaries"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Review covers the local working tree, which includes uncommitted changes. No production data or live payment provider was modified or validated. Gap tickets represent missing capability, policy or verification, not a claim of an exploited defect. Preserve immutable financial evidence, tenant isolation and existing working flows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Single-developer sprint sequence \u2014 2026-11-04"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Target candidate: AIN S11 | Safe regeneration and activation (Jira sprint 46)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sprint outcome: Connect effective financial revisions and preserve human corrections during regeneration."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Exit evidence: Stable semantic/entity matching survives reorder; material changes identify stale pricing/quotes/approvals; one effective revision and historical replay are proven."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Planning envelope: 6 implementation days + 2 integrated verification days + 1 review/refinement day + 1 contingency day; not measured velocity. One primary outcome in progress; at most two closely related workflow slices. Story/task pairs share effort, not double-counted work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Existing active sprint remains active with original dates; only its goal/name and unfinished membership are reorganized. Every new sprint is future and undated. No fabricated story-point/time estimates or assignees. The ordered slots are a provisional work breakdown, not a fixed delivery forecast. Before activation, split any candidate exceeding six implementation days and verify reviewer/provider readiness; preserve all parent acceptance criteria."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Scheduling is not implementation: original AC/DoD and parent scope are unchanged. Related story/task/subtask effort is one delivery slice, not additive capacity. Required domain slices can be delivered earlier than the broader owner completion sprint; no broader item is Done until all original requirements pass."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
